==Trivia==
* This [[Pikachu short]] was released alongside [[M16]]. However, as [[Jessie's Wobbuffet]] appears alongside [[Iris's Axew]] and [[Cilan's Pansage]], it does not fit into the series continuity and is likely intended to be non-[[canon]].
* This Pikachu short debuted in {{pmin|Indonesia}} and {{pmin|the Philippines}} before it did in {{pmin|the United States}}. It aired on November 2, 6, and 9, 2013, in Indonesia; and on November 13, 2013, in the Philippines.
* While cooking, {{MTR}} mentions that he is good at making noodles, which was first seen in ''[[DP117|Noodles! Roamin' Off!]]''.
* During the credits, Meowth and {{TP|Jessie|Wobbuffet}} make an ice sculpture of a {{p|Mime Jr.}} in reference to {{OP|James|Mime Jr.}}.
* An extended version of [[Let's Join Hands]] is used as the ending theme.

===Errors===
* When {{p|Umbreon}} uses {{m|Psychic}} on the watermelons, {{p|Vaporeon}}'s ears are fully white instead of yellow like they should be.

===Dub edits===
* The version of the Pikachu short used in [[Camp Pokémon]] cuts approximately two minutes of footage: when {{p|Glaceon}} uses {{m|Ice Shard}} on {{AP|Oshawott}}, when {{p|Leafeon}} uses {{m|Magical Leaf}} on Oshawott, the scene when {{p|Flareon}} is introduced, when Glaceon and Leafeon attack Meowth and Wobbuffet and they blast off, when Meowth and Wobbuffet climb up the cliff and blast off after being attacked by {{p|Sylveon}}, and when Meowth realizes {{p|Gothitelle}} wasn't intending to attack them. This is likely due to the fighting in the cut footage being considered inappropriate for the app's intended audience.

